                <invention-title lang="de">SIGNALISIERUNG ZUR MU-INTERFERENZMESSUNG MIT NZP-CSI-RS</invention-title>
                <invention-title lang="fr">SIGNALISATION POUR MESURE D'INTERFÉRENCE MU AVEC CSI-RS NZP</invention-title>
                <invention-title lang="en">SIGNALING FOR MU INTERFERENCE MEASUREMENT WITH NZP CSI-RS</invention-title>
            </bibliographic-data>
            <abstract lang="en">
                <p>A method performed by a wireless device (702) for performing measurements in a wireless communication system (700) is presented. The method comprises receiving (2400), from a network node (704) of the wireless communication system (700), a semi-static indication of one or more first sets of Non-Zero Power, NZP, Channel State Information Reference Signal, CSI-RS, resources for channel measurement and receiving (2402), from the network node (704), a semi-static indication of one or more second sets of NZP CSI-RS resources for interference measurement, wherein each of the one or more first sets of NZP CSI-RS resources consists of a single NZP CSI-RS resource associated with one or more CSI-RS ports, each of the one or more second sets of NZP CSI-RS resources consists of one or more NZP CSI-RS resources, and each CSI-RS port associated with the one or more second sets of NZP CSI-RS resources corresponds to a Multiple User Multiple Input Multiple Output, MU-MIMO, interference layer associated with a co-scheduled user equipment. The method further comprises receiving (2404, 2406), from the network node (704), one or more dynamic indications requesting a CSI report according to a first set of NZP CSI-RS resources from the one or more first sets of NZP CSI-RS resources for channel measurement and a second set of NZP CSI-RS resources from the one or more second sets of NZP CSI-RS resources for interference measurement. Further still, the method comprises reporting (2412), in the CSI report, results of the channel measurement and the interference measurement to the network node (704).</p>
            </abstract>
